{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculate the nth Bell number using dynamic programming with Stirling numbers of the second kind.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Create a 2D array to store Stirling numbers of the second kind\n    stirling = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Base cases\n    stirling[0][0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        stirling[i][0] = 0\n        stirling[i][i] = 1\n    \n    # Fill the Stirling numbers table using recurrence relation\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, min(i, n) + 1):\n            if i > j:\n                stirling[i][j] = j * stirling[i-1][j] + stirling[i-1][j-1]\n    \n    # Bell number is the sum of all Stirling numbers S(n, k) for k = 0 to n\n    bell = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        bell += stirling[n][k]\n    \n    return bell"}
