{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    \"\"\"Count sequences where each element >= 2*previous and <= m.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n    \n    # dp[i][j] = number of sequences of length i ending with value j\n    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Base case: sequences of length 1\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[1][j] = 1\n    \n    # Fill dp table\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            # Previous element must be <= j//2\n            for prev in range(1, j // 2 + 1):\n                dp[i][j] += dp[i-1][prev]\n    \n    # Sum all sequences of length n\n    return sum(dp[n][j] for j in range(1, m + 1))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the number of valid sequences of length n with elements <= m where each element >= 2 * previous.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n    \n    # dp[i][j] = number of sequences of length i ending with value j\n    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Base case: sequences of length 1\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[1][j] = 1\n    \n    # Fill dp table\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            # For each ending value j, sum all valid previous values\n            for prev in range(1, min(j // 2, m) + 1):\n                if 2 * prev <= j:\n                    dp[i][j] += dp[i-1][prev]\n    \n    # Sum all sequences of length n\n    return sum(dp[n][j] for j in range(1, m + 1))"}
