{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix):\n    n = len(matrix)\n    \n    # dp[i][j] stores (max_sum, path_length) for path ending at (i, j)\n    dp = [[(0, 0) for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n)]\n    dp[0][0] = (matrix[0][0], 1)\n    \n    # Fill first row\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        dp[0][j] = (dp[0][j-1][0] + matrix[0][j], dp[0][j-1][1] + 1)\n    \n    # Fill first column\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        dp[i][0] = (dp[i-1][0][0] + matrix[i][0], dp[i-1][0][1] + 1)\n    \n    # Fill rest of the matrix\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(1, n):\n            from_top = (dp[i-1][j][0] + matrix[i][j], dp[i-1][j][1] + 1)\n            from_left = (dp[i][j-1][0] + matrix[i][j], dp[i][j-1][1] + 1)\n            \n            avg_from_top = from_top[0] / from_top[1]\n            avg_from_left = from_left[0] / from_left[1]\n            \n            if avg_from_top >= avg_from_left:\n                dp[i][j] = from_top\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = from_left\n    \n    return dp[n-1][n-1][0] / dp[n-1][n-1][1]"}
